": "If national Democratic spending actually materializes and independent polling confirms single digits, the race could tighten toward Lean R.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Stephanie Bice (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Oklahoma's 5th District leans nine points Republican, and Rep. Stephanie Bice seeks another term with a large financial edge: roughly $2.0 million on hand to Democrat Jena Nelson's about $17,000. Ten ratings outlets place the race between Likely and Safe Republican, and prediction markets give Nelson roughly a one-in-seven chance. Bice, a Trump-endorsed incumbent, advanced easily through her primary and has a legislative record to run on.\n\nStill, there are faint signs of life for Democrats. A September poll from a Democratic-aligned firm had Bice up only five points, national Democrats have added the seat to their target list and discussed investing in it, and the midterm environment favors the opposition. Bice has so far declined to debate. Nelson needs outside money and a strong national wave to close a gap that the district's lean and her cash deficit currently make steep.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0558, "margin": -10.29}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0638, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1454, "margin": -7.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0909, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1152, "margin": -7.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0488, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.099, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.1151, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0881, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0678, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0911, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0833, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.097, "margin": -8.8}]}